  "reasoning": "This commit wrapped the OptimizeGloballyPopupExpertBatch action listener logic (which reads `getSavedFilteringAndGrouping()`) in a `new Thread(new Runnable(){...})`, making the global optimization run asynchronously. Before this change, the action executed synchronously, so nulling out `savedFilteringAndGrouping` right after triggering global optimization (in StitchingExplorerPanel) was safe. After this commit made global optimization asynchronous, the panel's code path (added earlier in 4516bc398890) that immediately sets `savedFilteringAndGrouping = null` right after calling `globalOptPopup.doClick()` now races with the async thread that still needs to read the saved value — exactly the race the fix commit addresses by deferring the discard until the async thread itself is done using it.",
